><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Athletes, coaches, and other staff involved in the training process&#xD;should be aware of the differences between tDCS setups and be&#xD;cautious when using it in a direct to consumer manner. Even though&#xD;studies have shown promising results about the beneficial effects of&#xD;tDCS on performance, the results of the present study suggest that&#xD;a-tDCS of the M1 does not improve aerobic performance in&#xD;complex sports-related tasks.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
